.TH tupkgfinder n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tupkgfinder
.PP
Inspect how Tcl resolves packages: known versions, their \fBifneeded\fR scripts and source locations, which version is active versus shadowed, the relevant search paths (\fBauto_path\fR, \fBtcl::tm::path\fR), and an optional filesystem search by glob pattern. \fBcandidates\fR and \fBshadows\fR (0.2) list every copy of a package on the search paths \-\- also a second copy with the same version, which the package database never shows because it keeps one \fBifneeded\fR per version. Useful for "about / diagnostics" views. Pure Tcl, no GUI.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::paths
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::versions       packageName
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::pkgInfo        packageName
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::which          packageName
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::report         packageName
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::findFileSystem pattern ?roots?
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::findFileSystem pattern ?-roots {d ...}? ?-maxdepth N? \
        ?-followlinks 0|1? ?-maxfiles N? ?-excludeDirs {name ...}?
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::candidates     ?-pattern glob? ?-tmpaths list? ?-autopath list?
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::shadows        ?-pattern glob? ?-all 0|1? ?-tmpaths list? ?-autopath list?
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fBpaths\fR — dict \fB{auto_path {pos path ...} tm_path {pos path ...}}\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBversions\fR — versions known to the package database (those with an \fBifneeded\fR entry; note the running interpreter's own \fBTcl\fR has none).
.IP \(bu
\fBpkgInfo\fR — dict with \fBpackage\fR, \fBversions\fR, \fBifneeded\fR per version, and the source \fBlocations\fR extracted from each \fBifneeded\fR script.
.IP \(bu
\fBwhich\fR — resolution view: \fBfound\fR (version/path/script), \fBactiveVersion\fR, \fBactivePath\fR, and \fBshadowed\fR paths. Determining the active version calls \fBpackage require\fR, which loads the package as a side effect.
.IP \(bu
\fBreport\fR — a human\-readable multi\-line diagnostic for one package.
.IP \(bu
\fBfindFileSystem\fR — glob the filesystem for matching files. Without \fB\-roots\fR a platform default set is scanned (can be slow); bound it with \fB\-maxdepth\fR / \fB\-maxfiles\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBcandidates\fR — list of dicts \fB{package version kind path}\fR for every copy: kind \fBtm\fR (path = the \fB.tm\fR file in a module path; \fBa/b/x\-1.0.tm\fR is \fBa::b::x\fR) or \fBpkgIndex\fR (path = a \fBpkgIndex.tcl\fR in an \fBauto_path\fR directory or one level below, as Tcl searches). Only literal \fBpackage ifneeded NAME VERSION\fR lines are seen. \fB\-tmpaths\fR / \fB\-autopath\fR replace the interpreter's paths.
.IP \(bu
\fBshadows\fR — one dict per package with more than one copy (every package with \fB\-all 1\fR): \fB{package active activePath duplicate candidates}\fR. Each candidate carries a \fBstatus\fR: \fBactive\fR (the copy \fBpackage require\fR takes), \fBsame version\fR (a second copy of the active version that is not used \-\- the case to look at), or \fBother version\fR. \fBduplicate\fR is 1 when a version has more than one copy. For a package whose copies are not all registered yet, an unsatisfiable \fBpackage require\fR runs Tcl's unknown handlers first; nothing is loaded.
.CS
puts [::tclutils::tupkgfinder::report tablelist]
set w [::tclutils::tupkgfinder::which Img]
puts "active: [dict get $w activePath]  shadowed: [dict get $w shadowed]"
::tclutils::tupkgfinder::findFileSystem *pdf4tcl* -roots [list $root] -maxdepth 4
foreach d [::tclutils::tupkgfinder::shadows] {
    if {[dict get $d duplicate]} { puts "twice: [dict get $d package]" }
}
.CE
.SS Errors
.PP
Carries \fB{TCLUTILS TUPKGFINDER OPTION}\fR for an unknown option or a bad option/value count in \fBfindFileSystem\fR, \fBcandidates\fR and \fBshadows\fR.
.PP
Version note: 0.2 adds \fBcandidates\fR and \fBshadows\fR; the 0.1 commands are unchanged.
.SS Demo
.CS
tclsh examples/demo-tupkgfinder.tcl
.CE
